</patcit><patcit ucid="US-5448332-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5448332</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5696623-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5696623</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>NIPPON KOGAKU KK</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>NISHI KENJI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NIKON CORPORATION</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NISHI, KENJI</last-name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>NISHI KENJI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NISHI, KENJI</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An exposure method, wherein a defocus quantity on the surface of a substrate to be exposed with respect to an image plane of a projection optical system is detected highly accurately even during exposing without lowering throughput much and focusing is made with an automatic focusing method. A first oblique-incident AF sensor including an illumination slit unit (54a) through an optical member (63a) and a second oblique-incident AF sensor including an illumination slit unit (54b) through an optical member (63b) are used to apply slit images (F1f, F2f) onto common measuring points and focus positions are measured respectively. One half of the difference between the two measured values is regarded as a drift and the drift is corrected for values measured by the AF sensors; the first or second AF sensor is then used to perform a focusing by the automatic focusing method.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un procédé d'exposition selon lequel on détecte avec une grande précision la quantité défocalisée de la surface d'un substrat par rapport au plan image d'un système optique de projection, même lors d'expositions sans réduction de débit et avec le procédé automatique de mise au point. On utilise un premier détecteur AF oblique-incident comportant une fente d'illumination (54a) traversant un élément optique (63a) et un deuxième détecteur AF oblique-incident comportant une fente d'illumination (54b) traversant un élément optique (63b) pour appliquer les images de la fente (F1f, F2f) sur les points communs de mesure, puis on mesure les positions respectives des foyers. La moitié de la différence entre les deux valeurs mesurées est considérée comme une dérive qui est corrigée des valeurs mesurées par les détecteurs AF. On utilise alors les deux détecteurs AF pour une mise au point automatique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>